# Guitar Assistant - Design Document

## Project Overview
Guitar Assistant is a local desktop application designed to help beginning guitar players learn songs from PDF guitar tabs. The app provides an enhanced visual experience with synchronized scrolling and finger position guidance to make learning easier and more intuitive.

## Core Problem Statement
Beginning guitar players often struggle with:
- Following along with static PDF tabs while playing
- Understanding where to place fingers on the fretboard
- Keeping pace with the song
- Manually scrolling through tabs mid-performance
- Getting feedback on whether they're playing correctly

## Target User
- Beginning to intermediate guitar players
- Users who have guitar tabs in PDF format
- Players looking for visual learning aids
- Musicians who want to practice at their own pace

## Key Features

### 1. PDF Import & Processing
**Description**: Import and parse PDF files containing guitar tablature.

**Requirements**:
- Support for standard PDF formats
- Extract tablature notation (6-line staff with numbers)
- Parse chord diagrams and notation
- Handle multi-page documents
- Support for both scanned and digital PDFs

**Technical Considerations**:
- PDF parsing library (PyMuPDF, pdf.js, or PDFBox)
- OCR capabilities for scanned tabs (Tesseract)
- Music notation recognition

### 2. Enhanced Visual Display - **HORIZONTAL SCROLLING** ✓

**Description**: Traditional tablature view with horizontal auto-scroll, highlighting, and finger position indicators.

**Features**:
- Large, readable tablature display with horizontal scrolling
- Current position highlighted with playhead indicator
- Upcoming notes preview (3-5 measures ahead visible)
- Finger position numbers overlaid on frets (1=index, 2=middle, 3=ring, 4=pinky)
- Color-coded finger positions for clarity
- Auto-scroll at adjustable speeds
- Manual scroll override with mouse/keyboard
- Smooth animation between positions

**Fretboard Reference Panel**:
- Companion fretboard diagram below tabs (not hybrid overlay)
- Shows current chord/note finger positions
- Clear finger numbering (1-4)
- Updates in real-time as tab scrolls

### 3. Interactive Fretboard Display

**Description**: Real-time visual representation of where to place fingers.

**Features**:
- Full fretboard diagram (typically 12-15 frets visible)
- Highlighted dots showing finger positions
- Color coding:
  - Index finger (e.g., blue)
  - Middle finger (e.g., green)
  - Ring finger (e.g., yellow)
  - Pinky (e.g., red)
- Fret numbers and string labels
- Open string indicators
- Muted string indicators (X)

### 4. Playback Controls

**Description**: Controls for navigating through the tab.

**Features**:
- Play/Pause
- Speed adjustment (25%, 50%, 75%, 100%, 125%, 150%)
- Loop section (mark start/end points)
- Skip to measure/section
- Metronome with adjustable tempo
- Click track to help with timing

### 5. Practice Mode

**Description**: Features specifically for practice and learning.

**Features**:
- Section markers (intro, verse, chorus, solo, etc.)
- Loop difficult sections infinitely
- Gradual speed increase (start slow, auto-increase when ready)
- Practice log/statistics
- Difficulty rating per section
- Notes/annotations on specific measures

### 6. Audio Input Recognition (Future Feature)

**Description**: Listen to guitar playing via microphone and provide feedback on accuracy.

**Requirements**:
- Microphone input capture
- Pitch detection algorithm
- String and fret identification from audio
- Real-time comparison with expected notes
- Visual feedback (correct/incorrect indicators)
- Timing accuracy measurement

**Technical Approaches**:
- Web Audio API (for web version)
- NAudio + pitch detection library (for desktop version)
- Consider ML models for better accuracy (e.g., CREPE for pitch detection)

**Note**: This is a Phase 3 feature, not required for MVP. No audio file playback needed.

