## Technical Architecture

### Technology Stack Options - **USER PREFERENCES: TypeScript or C#** ✓

#### Option 1: TypeScript Web App (RECOMMENDED)
**Pros**:
- Modern, responsive UI with React/Vue/Svelte
- Works offline as PWA (Progressive Web App)
- Cross-platform (Windows, Mac, Linux, mobile browsers)
- Rich ecosystem for UI components
- Good PDF.js support for parsing
- Web Audio API for future microphone input
- Easy to iterate and test
- No installation required

**Cons**:
- PDF parsing slightly more complex than desktop
- Browser security restrictions on file access

**Recommended Stack**:
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Framework**: React or Svelte (lightweight, fast)
- **Build Tool**: Vite (fast dev server, HMR)
- **PDF Processing**: PDF.js + custom tab parser
- **Graphics**: HTML Canvas or SVG for rendering
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS or styled-components
- **Audio Input**: Web Audio API (Phase 3)
- **State Management**: Zustand or Redux Toolkit
- **PWA**: Workbox for offline capabilities

#### Option 2: C# Desktop App (Alternative)
**Pros**:
- Native Windows performance
- Excellent PDF libraries (PdfSharp, iTextSharp)
- Strong typing and tooling
- NAudio for microphone input
- Professional-looking apps with WPF/Avalonia

**Cons**:
- Windows-focused (unless using Avalonia)
- Longer build times
- Distribution requires installer

**Recommended Stack**:
- **Language**: C# 12
- **Framework**: Avalonia UI (cross-platform) or WPF (Windows-only)
- **PDF Processing**: PdfSharp or iTextSharp
- **Graphics**: Skia (SkiaSharp) for rendering
- **Audio Input**: NAudio (Phase 3)
- **Build**: dotnet publish, ClickOnce installer

#### Option 3: Hybrid - Electron with TypeScript
**Pros**:
- Desktop app with web technologies
- Node.js backend for PDF processing
- Can use Python libraries via child processes if needed
- Better file system access than pure web

**Cons**:
- Larger bundle size (~150MB+)
- Higher memory usage

**Stack**:
- Electron + React + TypeScript
- PDF.js or pdf-lib
- Web Audio API

### Recommended Choice
**TypeScript Web App (React + Vite)** for MVP:
- Best balance of development speed and capability
- Works offline as PWA
- Modern UI patterns
- Easy to add Python backend later if needed for PDF parsing
- Can always wrap in Electron later if desktop features needed

