## Data Models

### Tab Structure
```python
class Tab:
    - song_title: str
    - artist: str
    - tuning: Tuning (E standard, Drop D, etc.)
    - tempo: int (BPM)
    - time_signature: str (4/4, 3/4, etc.)
    - measures: List[Measure]
    - sections: List[Section]

class Measure:
    - number: int
    - notes: List[Note]
    - duration: float

class Note:
    - string: int (1-6)
    - fret: int (0-24)
    - duration: float
    - technique: str (hammer-on, pull-off, bend, slide, etc.)
    - timestamp: float

class Section:
    - name: str (Intro, Verse, Chorus, etc.)
    - start_measure: int
    - end_measure: int
    - difficulty: int (1-5)

class Tuning:
    - strings: List[str] (E, A, D, G, B, E for standard)
```

