## Development Phases

### Phase 1: Core Functionality (MVP)
**Duration**: 3-4 weeks
- PDF upload and text extraction
- Tab parser (handle format from sample PDF)
- Horizontal scrolling tab display with Canvas/SVG
- Finger position indicators on tab
- Manual scroll controls (mouse, keyboard, touch)
- Basic fretboard reference panel
- Playhead position indicator
- **Deliverable**: Can load PDF, view tabs, manually scroll

### Phase 2: Auto-Scroll & Practice Features
**Duration**: 3-4 weeks
- Smooth auto-scrolling at variable speeds
- Play/pause controls
- BPM adjustment
- Section markers (intro, verse, chorus, etc.)
- Loop functionality for practice
- Speed adjustment (25%-200%)
- Keyboard shortcuts
- **Deliverable**: Full practice mode with auto-scroll

### Phase 3: Audio Input Recognition
**Duration**: 5-6 weeks
- Microphone input capture
- Pitch detection (Web Audio API + ML model)
- Note recognition and comparison
- Visual feedback for correct/incorrect notes
- Timing accuracy measurement
- Practice statistics
- **Deliverable**: Real-time playing feedback

### Phase 4: Enhancement & Polish
**Duration**: 2-3 weeks
- Theme customization (dark/light mode)
- Multiple tab format support
- Tab library management
- Export practice sessions
- Performance optimization
- PWA offline capabilities
- **Deliverable**: Production-ready application

## Challenges & Risks

### Technical Challenges
1. **PDF Parsing Accuracy**
   - Challenge: Tabs vary widely in format
   - Mitigation: Start with well-formatted digital PDFs, add format support incrementally
   - Alternative: Manual correction interface

2. **Real-time Performance**
   - Challenge: Smooth scrolling and rendering
   - Mitigation: Optimize rendering, consider hardware acceleration

3. **Tab Recognition**
   - Challenge: Converting PDF to structured data
   - Mitigation: Use regex patterns, consider ML for complex cases

### User Experience Challenges
1. **Learning Curve**
   - Risk: Too many features overwhelm beginners
   - Mitigation: Simple default mode, progressive feature disclosure

2. **PDF Compatibility**
   - Risk: Not all PDF tabs are compatible
   - Mitigation: Clear documentation of supported formats, conversion tools

## Success Metrics

- Successfully imports 80%+ of standard guitar tab PDFs
- Smooth scrolling at various speeds without lag
- Fretboard accurately shows finger positions
- Users can learn a song section 30% faster than with static PDF
- Application startup time < 3 seconds
- Memory usage < 200MB for typical tab

